11
00:58:18,000 --> 00:58:24,000
Little Boy is a 2015 World War II war-drama film
directed by Alejandro Gómez Monteverde.

12
01:03:36,000 --> 01:03:42,000
The screenplay is by Monteverde and Pepe Portillo, and the film was produced by Eduardo
Verástegui and Leo Severino, and edited by Joan Sobel and Fernando Villena.

13
01:08:54,000 --> 01:09:00,000
The film stars Jakob Salvati, Emily Watson, David Henrie, Cary-Hiroyuki Tagawa, Michael Rapaport, Ben Chaplin,
Eduardo Verástegui, Ted Levine, Abraham Benrubi, Toby Huss, Kevin James, and Tom Wilkinson.

14
01:14:12,000 --> 01:14:18,000
The title is a reference to Little Boy, the code name for the atomic bomb dropped on
Hiroshima, as well as a reference to the main character Pepper's height.

15
01:19:30,000 --> 01:19:36,000
The film was co-produced by Metanoia Films and Santa Fé Films and
was released on April 24, 2015, by Open Road Films.

16
01:24:48,000 --> 01:24:54,000
It was released on DVD and Blu-ray on August 18, 2015, by
Universal Pictures Home Entertainment.

17
01:30:06,000 --> 01:30:12,000
The film received negative reviews from mainstream critics and
earned $17 million on a $20 million budget.

18
01:35:24,000 --> 01:35:30,000
An Indian adaptation of the film, titled Tubelight and starring Salman Khan
in the lead role, also opened to negative reviews in 2017.

19
01:40:42,000 --> 01:40:48,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
